egin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\cdot {30}^{∘}+2\\cdot n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={60}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97786302-e865-5581-b08e-8da7c6b7a01b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb40ff3e-c133-59e3-84f4-c32e6d8e00b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290258} {:answer/id #uuid "3257e71f-bc3a-5aad-8c9c-ed9975d1e6ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290259} {:answer/id #uuid "33aeeb5d-a7cd-5364-81a6-21255fc05466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290260} {:answer/id #uuid "d1301c98-37d6-5d1f-a530-caeac34992f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290261} {:answer/id #uuid "51d05205-2a44-571c-9fe6-0a46d9bac4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1301c98-37d6-5d1f-a530-caeac34992f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290261} :answer-field/id #uuid "f174b471-39ba-50e0-8520-6820e09a1af1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5bb27746-8006-512c-b1d1-5ac0d202a97a" :question/math-academy-id "q-121066" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{18}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{18}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290263 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f05f92c8-c06b-5b18-919d-5c831c3ce26f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290265} {:answer/id #uuid "9d889096-41d0-5c10-a077-ffd7f30baffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290266} {:answer/id #uuid "46b832ec-3d9f-51ea-8063-fe283d499712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "480" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290267} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3fe27c-441f-529d-b735-ef4dcc98582b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "450" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290268} {:answer/id #uuid "dba553fe-eba7-5d9b-ad97-eb008720e333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dba553fe-eba7-5d9b-ad97-eb008720e333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "360" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290269} :answer-field/id #uuid "9682efdf-8129-5464-ac1f-474669f9712e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "af7a00ee-e00a-5214-8f02-2d3a8d990809" :question/math-academy-id "q-121071" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric  equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx={180}^{∘}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{∘},\\,x={a}^{∘}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,\\frac{x}{3}={120}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\nx={180}^{∘}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{∘},\\,x={360}^{∘}+n\\cdot 1\\,{080}^{∘}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=360.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290270 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "482b154a-40f1-5b5b-9192-9af9578e1894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290272} {:answer/id #uuid "c32dfffc-2fae-52b4-928e-0099368ae85c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290273} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f05c12-5052-5fda-bec8-69757ed59cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290274} {:answer/id #uuid "127f7b02-f854-572f-af19-d72c7aaa02e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290275} {:answer/id #uuid "722313b2-8c80-5584-87d7-95808b5eff80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "722313b2-8c80-5584-87d7-95808b5eff80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290276} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec4963a7-b35b-5b1e-8360-9996abfaac59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9bc4a944-f7ef-59d9-81e2-47ad1c9030d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-17357" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x+{50}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=-{1}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘},\\,x={b}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $b?$" :question/worked-solution "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+{50}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 5x+{50}^{∘} & ={315}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & =-{5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={265}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & =-{1}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={53}^{∘}+n\\cdot {72}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=53.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ea83062-5744-52ef-9b3e-f9805ed092fb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86654b7b-321e-5fc5-8363-d6be7b49633a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290279} {:answer/id #uuid "f7aa660e-6667-5069-9a21-dfa590da3b93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290280} {:answer/id #uuid "c38864d9-2c28-5e77-a147-d1c9518d7ec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290281} {:answer/id #uuid "d77e274e-acdc-5e25-9edc-a553bb6e1f36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290282} {:answer/id #uuid "f55b8f6b-06b7-50bf-a065-0ff2ceca6393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d77e274e-acdc-5e25-9edc-a553bb6e1f36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290282} :answer-field/id #uuid "22c0d1fb-d761-50e5-9913-a051fda7b196" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91d134db-5dc7-5deb-b61f-68fd3c27cbb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-42790" :question/problem "Consider the following trigonometric  equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{12})=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a+6\\pi n,\\,x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+6\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{12})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{12}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi ,\\,\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{12}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{12}-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi , & \\,\\frac{x}{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{12}-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}=-\\frac{7\\pi }{12}+2n\\pi , & \\,\\frac{x}{3}=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x=-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+6n\\pi , & \\,x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+6n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.$"}]}
